    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "If I showed you documentation from the hospital and the people involved that clearly explained everything about your father's death, and it all made sense, would you be able to accept that explanation, or would you still believe something was being hidden?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, if you showed me documentation... I mean, I've already seen the documents they *want* me to see. It’s honestly exactly like dealing with my internet service provider. They send you these automated diagnostic reports saying your connection is fine, everything's green on their end. Do you know how hard it is to get a Level 2 technician on the phone now? You sit on hold for hours listening to that terrible royalty-free jazz, and when someone finally picks up, they just read from a script. I had to threaten to cancel my service entirely last month just to get them to admit there was a node outage in my neighborhood. They'll just tell you whatever gets you off the phone, you know? \n\nSo, when you ask if I'd just accept their explanation... I know everyone keeps telling me the hospital records and those donation emails all line up. My sister thinks it's an open-and-shut case. But when I actually compare the timestamps on those files, and I factor in the missing email attachments... and then you look at the way certain community members just completely avoid my questions when I bring it up? It’s obvious to me. Someone is hiding what really happened around my father’s death. You can show me all the paperwork you want, but they're just trying to get me off the phone, so to speak.",
