    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "If multiple independent experts—like hospital administrators, forensic accountants, and cybersecurity specialists—all reviewed the exact same evidence you've looked at and concluded there was no cover-up, would that change your mind at all, or would you believe they were also part of the deception?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Independent experts? I mean, who pays these experts? It's always a web of contracts and consulting fees if you dig deep enough. It's like... okay, so last year, I decided I wanted to get into hydroponic gardening. I live in an apartment, so space is tight, but I figured I could grow some tomatoes on the balcony. I spent weeks researching nutrient solutions, and every \"independent expert\" blog recommended this one specific brand of liquid fertilizer. So I bought it, right? Thirty bucks a bottle. And my plants just withered. Total root rot. It wasn't until I checked the WHOIS data on those blogs that I realized they were all registered to the same parent company that manufactured the fertilizer. It's all vertical integration. I ended up just using compost I got from a community garden down the street. The tomatoes were okay, a little small, but at least I knew what was in the soil. \n\nSo when you talk about these experts reviewing the data... I've already done the work. I know everyone keeps telling me the hospital records and the donation emails all line up perfectly. They all want to say it's a closed book. But when I actually sit down and compare the timestamps on those files, and I factor in those missing attachments, plus the way certain community members completely avoid my questions when I bring it up? It’s obvious to me. Someone is hiding what really happened around my father’s death. Bringing in more people to look at the same tampered evidence isn't going to change the facts. It just adds more people to the payroll.",
